[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   step_165: canonical disformal transport -- amplitude closure for
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   the comet boundary slip (b131).
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   Step 158 (b124) established that a single-valued scalar winding
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   realisation cannot produce the slip: d(phi) is exact, the physical
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   endpoint term is leg-symmetric, and the tested open-path statistic
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   was cap-blind.  The canonical theory paper (0-TEP, Jakarta revision,
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   Sec. 3.3 / 6 / A3.2) supplies the structure that step was missing:
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   the invariant observable is the synchronisation connection
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   dsigma_mu = -(B/A^2)(u . grad phi) P_mu^nu grad_nu phi ,
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   whose scalar (conformal) part is exact and whose leading NON-exact
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   part is the projected disformal term.  A comet is a transported
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   clock: along its worldline u.grad phi = du/dt, so the open-path
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   desynchronisation relative to the barycentric network is
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   dt_slip = (1/c) int dsigma_i dx^i
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   = -(1/c^2) int b(u) R_H^2 / (A^2 N^2) (du/dt)^2 dt
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   with the corpus field-space envelope (excursion convention: u is the
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   field measured from the contemporary ambient; the absolute-u convention
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   is macroscopically excluded in the Paper-0 triangle calculation)
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   b(u) = B0 * u^2/(1+u^2) * exp(-u^4 / 2 sigma_B^4),
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   B0 = +3.2e-3   (admissible-branch benchmark).  The magnitude is
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   mirrored from the Paper-0 volume-balance reconstruction only to
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   set an instrumental scale; that reconstruction found B0 < 0 and
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   is excluded by the Paper-0 null-cone condition.  It is therefore
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   not a calibration of the admissible normalization.
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   The primary step-065 datum is an equivalent-time amplitude obtained
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   from an angular separation, delta t_eq = |delta theta| r_b^2/h.  It is
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   unsigned.  Consequently the fit below must use |delta t_slip|.  The
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   sign of the open-path synchronization transport is retained separately
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   and is never inferred from that amplitude statistic.
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   Properties that follow from the form alone (all measured
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   independently in this pipeline):
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   * sign-definite in B: one sign of slip, no tuned sign;
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   * quadratic in the traversal rate -> the slip concentrates where
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   |grad u| is concentrated: a boundary transition gives a discrete
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   crossing offset (step 071 shell flatness, step 068 transit-time
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   independence);
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   * the comet crosses the boundary twice, at antipodal points, so an
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   axis-anchored field G(th) contributes G(th)^4 + G(180-th)^4 --
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   every odd harmonic cancels identically and the open-path slip is
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   automatically bipolar (cos 2th dominated) for ANY axis-anchored
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   field -- the morphology the residual slip field actually carries
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   (step 086: cos2th rho=+0.17, p=0.010; cos th flat at p=0.30),
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   while the resident-cloud source response is linear and stays
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   dipolar (step 164);
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   * the theta-uniform part of the lag is absorbed into the fitted
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   elements (parameter absorption, step 151) -- the observable is
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   the theta-dependent contrast, which is what the harmonic map
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   measures.
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   The open question tested quantitatively: at a positive-B admissible
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   benchmark of the same magnitude as the excluded reconstruction scale,
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   what boundary field excursion u_b does the measured amplitude contrast
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   require?  The answer is a scale relation, not a normalization
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   prediction, and is compared against the corpus anchors
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   (Newtonian-tracking 4e-11, Galactic ambient ~7e-7, solar surface ~2e-6,
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   cosmological u ~ 0.75).
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   Channels:
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   M (motion/quadratic): u.grad phi = du/dt along the comet
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   worldline -> per-crossing lag ~ (|B0| R_H^2/c^2) v_r *
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   int env_b(u) (du/dr)^2 dr; bipolar response via the
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   antipodal sum (exact for every axis-anchored G).
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   R (network roll): u.grad phi = -Pi W (partitioned roll of the
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   static clock congruence, Pi = H0) -> net transport
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   ~ (|B0| R_H^2/c^2) Pi * [U(G_in) - U(G_out)], signed by the
[2026-09-24 10:52:07 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   antipodal field difference; dipolar response, subdominant.
